+<h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p class="lede">What personal information we use, why, and your rights.</p></div></section>
+<article class="art"><div class="in">
+<h2 id="contact">Who we are</h2><p>ZANS Racing Tools &amp; Gifts, Leicester, England runs this website and the ZANSRacingTools shop on Etsy. [EMAIL ADDRESS NEEDED FROM ALEX]. Or <a href="https://www.etsy.com/uk/shop/ZANSRacingTools" target="_blank" rel="noopener">message us through our Etsy shop</a> (Message seller on the shop page or on your order).</p>
+<h2>What this website collects</h2><p>This website has no accounts, forms or checkout, and does not ask for your name, email or payment details. It uses the Metricool tracker to count visits and see which pages are viewed and where visitors come from (for example the page, referring site and type of device). We use this only to understand and improve the website.</p><p>The mug and bauble designers keep the design you are working on in your own browser&#39;s storage so it is still there if you come back. It is not sent to us. You can clear it by clearing your browser data.</p>
+<h2>Orders on Etsy</h2><p>When you buy from us on Etsy, Etsy handles the payment and shares with us what we need to fulfil the order: your name, delivery address, the items and options you chose, and any messages you send. Etsy&#39;s own privacy policy covers how Etsy uses your data.</p><p>We use your order details only to make, send and support your order and to keep the business records the law requires. For printed items we share your name, delivery address and the design with the print partner that makes and posts the item, only for that purpose.</p>
+<h2>Legal basis and how long we keep it</h2><p>We use order information to perform our contract with you and to meet legal obligations such as tax records. We use website visit statistics for our legitimate interest in running the website. We keep order records for as long as the law requires for accounting, normally 6 years, and nothing longer than we need.</p>
+<h2>Your rights</h2><p>Under UK data protection law you can ask for a copy of the personal information we hold about you, and ask us to correct it, delete it or stop using it. Contact us using the details above. If you are unhappy with how we handle your information you can complain to the Information Commissioner&#39;s Office (ICO), ico.org.uk.</p>
+<h2>Links to other websites</h2><p>Our pages link to Etsy and to our social media pages. Those sites have their own privacy policies.</p>
+<p><i>Last updated: 24 November 2026.</i></p>
